Jump to search</a>
				<!-- start content -->
				<div id=3D"mw-content-text" class=3D"mw-body-content"><div class=3D"mw-=
content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang=3D"en" dir=3D"ltr"><p>There are two type=
s of <b>mirroring</b> on the NES:
</p>
<ul><li><b><a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/Mirroring#Memory_Mirrorin=
g">Memory Mirroring</a></b> is when the same memory may be accessed at mult=
iple addresses, causing an apparent duplication.</li>
<li><b><a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/Mirroring#Nametable_Mirroring=
">Nametable Mirroring</a></b> describes the layout of the NES' 2x2 <a href=
=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/PPU_nametables" title=3D"PPU nametables">ba=
ckground nametable</a> graphics, usually achieved by mirrored memory.</li><=
/ul>
<p><br>
</p>
