_mirroring_diagram.png" class=3D"mw-file-description" title=3D"1-screen fix=
ed"><img alt=3D"1-screen fixed" src=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/w/images/defa=
ult/thumb/c/c4/Single_screen_2000_mirroring_diagram.png/120px-Single_screen=
_2000_mirroring_diagram.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"120" height=3D"113=
" class=3D"mw-file-element"></a></span></div>
			<div class=3D"gallerytext">1-screen fixed</div>
		</li>
</ul>
<p>Other uncommon types of mirroring are available in other boards, such as=
 <a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/INES_Mapper_119" title=3D"INES Mapp=
er 119">TxSROM</a> variations of the MMC3, extended techniques available to=
 the <a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/MMC5" title=3D"MMC5">MMC5</a>, =
arbitrary VRAM mirroring arrangements by the <a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.=
org/wiki/Namco_163" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Namco 163">Namco 163</a>=
, or ROM mirroring arrangements using mappers that allow <a href=3D"https:/=
/www.nesdev.org/wiki/Category:Mappers_with_ROM_nametables" title=3D"Categor=
y:Mappers with ROM nametables">ROM nametables</a>.
</p><p><b>Diagonal mirroring</b> (CIRAM A10 =3D PA11 XOR PA10) would facili=
tate changes in scrolling direction without having to flip between Horizont=
al and Vertical mirroring.
</p><p><b>L-shaped mirroring</b> (CIRAM A10 =3D PA11 OR PA10), seen in Sach=
en's <a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/INES_Mapper_243" title=3D"INES =
Mapper 243">374N</a> and <a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/Sachen_8259=
" title=3D"Sachen 8259">8259 family</a>, allows scrolling in four direction=
s as long as scrolling changes directions only at screen boundaries.
</p><p>Unusual cases:
</p>
<ul><li><i>Castlevania 3</i> uses the third nametable RAM available on the =
<a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/MMC5" title=3D"MMC5">MMC5</a> (<a hr=
ef=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/File:Castlevania_III_3-Screen_Mirroring.p=
ng" title=3D"File:Castlevania III 3-Screen Mirroring.png">illustration</a>)=
</li>
<li><i>Laser Invasion</i> uses the third nametable RAM available on the <a =
href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/MMC5" title=3D"MMC5">MMC5</a></li>
<li><i>After Burner</i> uses the ROM nametables available on the <a href=3D=
"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/INES_Mapper_068" title=3D"INES Mapper 068">Sun=
soft-4</a> (iNES 68), but it only supports 1/H/V arrangements.</li>
<li><i>Mighty Morphin Power Rangers III, IV (JY Company)</i> uses ROM namet=
ables in a 3-Screen horizontal configuration, though the lower screen is ne=
ver shown (But, lower screen has been used in the status bar).</li></ul>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id=3D"Mirroring_chart">Mirroring =
chart</h3></div>
<p>This table lists the more simple and easy to understand mirroring and sc=
rolling techniques. There are a huge variety of more complicated techniques=
. For a more comprehensive survey, see: <a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/w=
iki/List_of_games_by_mirroring_technique" title=3D"List of games by mirrori=
ng technique">List of games by mirroring technique</a>
</p>
<table class=3D"wikitable">
<tbody><tr>
<th>Scrolling Type</th>
<th>Mirroring</th>
<th>Example Games</th>
<th>Comment
</th></tr>
<tr>
<td>None
</td>
<td>Any
</td>
<td><i>Donkey Kong</i>, <i>Tennis</i>
</td>
<td>With only a single fixed screen, any mirroring type can be used.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>Horizontal Only
</td>
<td>Vertical
</td>
<td><i>Super Mario Bros.</i>, <i>Gimmick!</i>
</td>
<td>A <a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/w/index.php?title=3DStatus_bar&amp;=
action=3Dedit&amp;redlink=3D1" class=3D"new" title=3D"Status bar (page does=
 not exist)">status bar</a> at the top is easy to accomplish with a <a href=
=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/Sprite-0_hit" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=
=3D"Sprite-0 hit">sprite-0 hit</a> (see <i>Super Mario Bros.</i>).
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>Vertical Only
</td>
<td>Horizontal
</td>
<td><i>Ice Climber</i>, <i>Gun.Smoke</i>
</td>
<td>Without a status bar, horizontal mirroring is the best choice for verti=
cal-only scrolling. With a status bar, vertical or single-screen mirroring =
give you a place in the nametable to render the status bar, and the scrolli=
ng seam should be hidden under the bar.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>Alternating Horizontal/Vertical
</td>
<td>Mapper switches H/V
</td>
<td><i>Metroid</i>, <i>Air Fortress</i>
</td>
<td>Motion is limited to a single axis at any given time, and the direction=
 can only change when a new screen is reached.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>Limited Bidirectional
</td>
<td>Horizontal/Vertical
</td>
<td><i>Super Mario Bros. 3</i>, <i>Fire Emblem</i>
</td>
<td>By limiting one of the scrolling axes to only 2-screens wide, this make=
s unlimited scrolling in the other axis simple. With unlimited horizontal s=
crolling there will be unavoidable attribute glitches at one side of the sc=
reen (see <i>Super Mario Bros. 3</i>), but with unlimited vertical scrollin=
g this can be hidden by <a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/Overscan" ti=
tle=3D"Overscan">overscan</a> in NTSC regions (see <i>Fire Emblem</i>).
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>Unlimited Bidirectional
</td>
<td>Various
</td>
<td><i>Castlevania II</i>, <i>Battletoads</i>, <i>Crystalis</i>, <i>Final F=
antasy</i>
</td>
<td>Unlimited scrolling in both axes at once is an advanced technique requi=
ring a game-specific solution.
</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>The best way to understand the mirroring techniques used in a game, use =
a debugging emulator to look at the nametables. <a href=3D"https://www.nesd=
ev.org/w/index.php?title=3DStatus_bar&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;redlink=3D1" cl=
ass=3D"new" title=3D"Status bar (page does not exist)">Status bars</a> typi=
cally require a scrolling split at a timed location on the screen. This can=
 be done most easily with a mapper based <a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/=
wiki/IRQ" title=3D"IRQ">IRQ</a>, but can also be accomplished with a <a hre=
f=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/Sprite-0_hit" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=
=3D"Sprite-0 hit">sprite-0 hit</a> or other techniques.
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id=3D"See_also">See also</h2></di=
v>
<ul><li><a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/PPU_scrolling" title=3D"PPU =
scrolling">PPU scrolling</a></li></ul>
